{:edb/db-before-t 2300 :edb/db-after-t 2301 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535613 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:38:56.169Z" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124235 1100 "If $A$ is a $9 \\times 11$ matrix that has $9$ pivot columns, then what is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$?" 13194139535613 false] [17592186124235 1100 "If $A$ is a $9 \\times 11$ matrix that has $9$ pivot columns, then what is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))?$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124235 1145 "We know that $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A$.\n\nSince $A$ has $11$ columns and $9$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is\n$11-9=2$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2\n$$\n\n." 13194139535613 false] [17592186124235 1145 "We know that $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A$. \n\nSince $A$ has $11$ columns and $9$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n11-9=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$." 13194139535613 true] [17592186124236 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/62cc7238e6676b8a43d216ab6c8b30504602c68fd548832eceac9b710b885471.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/b85d717afa8af39d10517f909a09b53e6d379beef6e04e3d9ce7d3e48c88dca4.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/8e12a5386c3db2149324bd28c174a5410f7751e0c963cf80969e0cfdf14e5d7b.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124236 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. If $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n2. If $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n3. If $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" 13194139535613 false] [17592186124236 1145 "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix.\n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1$.\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=2$.\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$nd column). So, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139535613 false] [17592186124236 1145 "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139535613 true] [17592186124237 1100 "Given ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/e20df1b44d2bfe100499eebfb4d2bdf8c1055978fdccbe11c8b5c0882052ace8.png) what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124237 1100 "Given $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)$?" 13194139535613 false] [17592186124237 1145 "To find $\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{3} &:=R_{3} + 3R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{4} \\mid:=R_{4} + 3R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column).\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A)) = 1\n$$" 13194139535613 false] [17592186124237 1145 "To find $\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A)) = 1.\n$$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124429 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357543 13194139535613 true] [17592186124429 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357550 13194139535613 true] [17592186124429 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357613 13194139535613 true] [17592186124430 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357557 13194139535613 true] [17592186124430 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357571 13194139535613 true] [17592186124430 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357592 13194139535613 true] [17592186124430 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357599 13194139535613 true] [17592186124431 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357564 13194139535613 true] [17592186124431 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357578 13194139535613 true] [17592186124431 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357585 13194139535613 true] [17592186124431 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357606 13194139535613 true] [17592186124780 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535613 true] [17592186124780 1100 "Let $R$ be a $8 \\cdot 12$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $R$?" 13194139535613 false] [17592186124780 1100 "Let $R$ be a $8\\times 12$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $R?$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124780 1145 "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(R))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $R.$ \n\nSince $R$ has $12$ columns and $8$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $R$ is \n\n$$\n12-8=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(R))=4.$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124781 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535613 true] [17592186124781 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124781 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. If $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ then $dim(Null(A)) = 0$.\n2. If $B = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $dim(Null(B)) = 2$.\n3. If $C = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $dim(Null(C)) = 1$." 13194139535613 false] [17592186124781 1145 "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124792 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535613 true] [17592186124792 1100 "If $D = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$, then $nullity(D) =$" 13194139535613 false] [17592186124792 1100 "If $D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(D)=$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186124792 1145 "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(D)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D))$, we reduce $D$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(D)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D))=0.\n$$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186125141 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535613 true] [17592186125141 1100 "If $A$ is a $5 \\cdot 8$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns, then $dim(Null(A)) =$" 13194139535613 false] [17592186125141 1100 "If $A$ is a $5\\times 8$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186125141 1145 "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A.$\n\nSince we are told that $A$ has $3$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=3.\n$$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186357543 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357544 13194139535613 true] [17592186357543 1089 "q-139969" 13194139535613 true] [17592186357543 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535613 true] [17592186357543 1100 "If $B$ is a $7\\times 12$ matrix that has $4$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186357543 1113 #uuid "4af574b7-0048-5ded-b921-a3f394b65c95" 13194139535613 true] [17592186357543 1145 "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(B))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $B.$\n\nSince we are told that $B$ has $4$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=4.\n$$" 13194139535613 true] [17592186357544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357545 13194139535613 true] [17592186357544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357546 13194139535613 true] [17592186357544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357547 13194139535613 true] [17592186357544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357548 13194139535613 true] [17592186357544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357549 13194139535613 true] [17592186357544 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535613 true] [17592186357544 1041 "selection" 13194139535613 true] [17592186357544 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357548 13194139535613 true] [17592186357544 1110 #uuid "20286e89-3eb5-5fc8-ba79-3a7e0f584a2e" 13194139535613 true] [17592186357545 1034 "3" 13194139535613 true] [175921863575